{{ElectionsCA}}

The '''2026 Los Angeles mayoral election''' was held on November 3, 2026, to elect the [[mayor of Los Angeles]], California.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Dates and Deadlines |website=Close the Gap California |url=https://closethegapca.org/dates-and-deadlines/ |access-date=May 22, 2024}}</ref> A nonpartisan [[top-two primary]] was held on June 2, 2026. Incumbent mayor [[Karen Bass]] announced her re-election bid in July 2024.<ref name=BassLaunch /> In the June 8 primary, Bass and city councilmember [[Nithya Raman]] advanced to the general election. Raman defeated Bass in the November general election.<ref name="defeats">{{Cite web |date=2026-11-05 |title=Nithya Raman defeats Bass to become next L.A. mayor |url=https://www.latimes.com/california/story/2026-11-05/nithya-raman-defeats-bass-to-become-next-la-mayor |access-date=2026-11-05 |website=[[Los Angeles Times]]|language=en}}</ref>

